  "reason": "The evidence strongly favors scvi_n200 as the RNA encoder (0.721-0.725 acc vs 0.52-0.60 for scgpt/pca_n2000), with transformer aggregation, multiprofile, and weighted fusion all performing well. The current best (config_040, 0.725) uses imagenet_vit_l, but we have not yet tested whether resnet50 could be competitive or superior as the image encoder. Config_048 (scvi_n200, resnet50, transformer, weighted) is the most direct single-variable comparison to our best result, changing only the image encoder. This is the best use of experiment 6 because: (1) it exploits the strong scvi_n200 + transformer + weighted signal, (2) it resolves the largest remaining uncertainty about the image backbone, and (3) with 4 experiments left, knowing whether resnet50 is viable determines whether to explore resnet50-based combinations or double down on imagenet_vit_l variants (e.g., avgpool aggregation) in the remaining budget."
}

